<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qaqortoq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Julianehåb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qaqortoq, formerly Julianehåb, is the largest town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a>, founded as a Danish trading post in 1775. It lies in the area of the medieval Norse <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-settlement">Eastern Settlement</a>, whose best-preserved ruin, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hvalsey-church">Hvalsey Church</a>, is nearby. It is a centre of fishing, sealskin processing and education for southern Greenland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qaqortoq.jpg" alt="Qaqortoq" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gregor Julien Straube · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qaqortoq_Market_Square.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
